    "TREATMENT": {
      "present": true,
      "status": "content",
      "content_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Initial response to lower amounts of fiber supplementation or use of other types of fiber is not as successful.",
          "pdf_page": 611,
          "printed_page": 529,
          "column": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "After 2–3 months without diarrhea, the amount of fiber can be slowly reduced successfully in approximately 50% of dogs.",
          "pdf_page": 611,
          "printed_page": 529,
          "column": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "After resolution of diarrhea with psyllium supplementation, owners may attempt to switch to a commercial high-fiber (insoluble fiber) diet that may be more convenient to feed; however diarrhea may return in 50% of dogs. Insoluble dietary fiber helps to distend the colonic lumen; distention is necessary for normal fecal storage and colonic motility. supplementation, owners may be able to switch from the highly digestible “GI” diet to a high-quality maintenance dog food.",
          "pdf_page": 611,
          "printed_page": 529,
          "column": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Lack of initial response to fiber supple mentation suggests that chronic idiopathic large bowel diarrhea may be due to irritable bowel syndrome, and pharmacologic management of that disorder should be instituted.",
          "pdf_page": 611,
          "printed_page": 529,
          "column": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "There is no known zoonotic potential.",
          "pdf_page": 611,
          "printed_page": 529,
          "column": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "There are no special considerations regarding pregnancy, fertility, or breeding.",
          "pdf_page": 611,
          "printed_page": 529,
          "column": 3
        }
      ],
